# Laravel Rules — Always Apply

## Architecture
```
Route → Controller (THIN) → Service (logic) → Repository (data) → DB
                          ↓
                    FormRequest (validate) + API Resource (transform)
```

## ✅ Thin Controller
```php
class UserController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(private UserService $userService) {}

    public function store(CreateUserRequest $request): JsonResponse
    {
        $user = $this->userService->create($request->validated());
        return new UserResource($user);
    }
}
// ❌ No business logic, no Eloquent, no validation in controllers!
```

## ✅ Service (business logic)
```php
class UserService
{
    public function __construct(private UserRepository $userRepository) {}

    public function create(array $data): User
    {
        if ($this->userRepository->findByEmail($data['email'])) {
            throw new AppException('Email already in use', 409, 'EMAIL_CONFLICT');
        }
        $data['password'] = Hash::make($data['password']);
        return $this->userRepository->create($data);
    }
}
```

## ✅ FormRequest (always, never $request->validate())
```php
class CreateUserRequest extends FormRequest
{
    public function authorize(): bool { return true; }
    public function rules(): array
    {
        return [
            'email'    => ['required', 'email', 'max:255', 'unique:users,email'],
            'name'     => ['required', 'string', 'min:2', 'max:100'],
            'password' => ['required', 'string', 'min:8'],
        ];
    }
}
```

## ✅ Eloquent ORM (never raw SQL concatenation)
```php
User::where('is_active', true)->orderByDesc('created_at')->paginate(20);
Order::with(['user', 'items.product'])->findOrFail($id);
```

## ✅ API Resource (always transform responses)
```php
class UserResource extends JsonResource
{
    public function toArray(Request $request): array
    {
        return ['id' => $this->id, 'name' => $this->name, 'email' => $this->email];
    }
}
// return new UserResource($user);
// return UserResource::collection($users);
```

## ✅ Model Must Have
```php
protected $fillable = ['name', 'email', 'password'];  // mass assignment
protected $hidden   = ['password', 'remember_token'];
protected $casts    = ['password' => 'hashed', 'email_verified_at' => 'datetime'];
```

## Checklist
- [ ] Controller delegating to Service (thin)
- [ ] FormRequest for validation
- [ ] API Resource for response
- [ ] Eloquent model has `$fillable`
- [ ] Business logic ONLY in Service
- [ ] `auth:sanctum` on protected routes
